<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">💡</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>Self-study quiz.</strong> This quiz is for your own review — answers are not recorded. You’ll get instant feedback on each question.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="quiz"><div class="quiz__top-bar"><div class="quiz__score-tracker" style="display:none;"></div><button class="quiz__start-over" type="button" style="display:none;">Start Over</button></div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q1b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">1</span> Michelangelo's Creation of Adam on the Sistine Chapel ceiling is a fresco. What is distinctive about fresco as a medium?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1a" id="q1a">
        <label for="q1a">Pigment is bound with egg yolk on a wooden panel.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1b" id="q1b">
        <label for="q1b">Pigment is applied to wet plaster, so the painting becomes part of the wall itself.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1c" id="q1c">
        <label for="q1c">Pigment is mixed with oil and layered slowly on canvas.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q1" value="q1d" id="q1d">
        <label for="q1d">The painting is made on translucent paper.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Because the pigment sinks into wet plaster and becomes part of the wall, frescoes can last for centuries. That is why Michelangelo's ceiling has survived for five hundred years.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Think about the word fresh. In fresco the pigment goes onto fresh, wet plaster and becomes part of the wall, which is why it lasts.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q2c">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">2</span> Why does oil paint give a painter the greatest range of color, texture, and detail?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2a" id="q2a">
        <label for="q2a">It is translucent, so the white paper shows through.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2b" id="q2b">
        <label for="q2b">It dries so quickly that no changes are possible.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2c" id="q2c">
        <label for="q2c">It dries slowly and can be layered, so the painter can blend, rework, and build up surfaces.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q2" value="q2d" id="q2d">
        <label for="q2d">It cannot be mixed with other colors.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Oil's slow drying and layering are part of what makes a Rembrandt self-portrait feel alive: the paint can model soft shadow and thick highlights.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The key properties of oil paint are slow drying and the ability to be layered. Look for the answer that treats those as advantages.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q3d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">3</span> A closed line in a painting is</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3a" id="q3a">
        <label for="q3a">always straight.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3b" id="q3b">
        <label for="q3b">soft, blurry, and suggested.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3c" id="q3c">
        <label for="q3c">invisible.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q3" value="q3d" id="q3d">
        <label for="q3d">hard, sharp, and definite.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Closed lines define edges firmly; open lines are soft and suggested. Lawrence's Migration Series uses closed lines; Rothko's soft edges are almost the opposite.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Closed and open describe how definite a line is. A closed line is hard and sharp; an open line is soft and suggested.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q4b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">4</span> Which three qualities describe a color?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4a" id="q4a">
        <label for="q4a">Primary, secondary, and tertiary.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4b" id="q4b">
        <label for="q4b">Hue, saturation, and value.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4c" id="q4c">
        <label for="q4c">Line, shape, and texture.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q4" value="q4d" id="q4d">
        <label for="q4d">Warm, cold, and neutral only.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Hue is the name of the color, saturation is its purity or intensity, and value is its lightness or darkness.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">The three qualities are hue (the color's name), saturation (its intensity), and value (how light or dark it is).</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q5a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">5</span> Van Gogh's The Starry Night has heavy, visible brushstrokes that create ridges on the surface. Which element of painting is this?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5a" id="q5a">
        <label for="q5a">Texture.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5b" id="q5b">
        <label for="q5b">Subject matter.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5c" id="q5c">
        <label for="q5c">Perspective drawing.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q5" value="q5d" id="q5d">
        <label for="q5d">Hue.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Texture is the surface quality of a painting. Oil can be applied thickly, so the brushstrokes become part of what you see.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Texture is the surface quality of the painting, here the ridges left by thick brushstrokes.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q6c">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">6</span> What does the lesson mean by the "all-at-onceness" of painting?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6a" id="q6a">
        <label for="q6a">A painting must be seen in a single second.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6b" id="q6b">
        <label for="q6b">Every painting contains all the colors of the rainbow.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6c" id="q6c">
        <label for="q6c">A painting presents everything simultaneously, with no sequence, and the viewer chooses where to look.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q6" value="q6d" id="q6d">
        <label for="q6d">A painting is always made in one sitting.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Unlike music, literature, or film, a painting offers all its elements immediately. The challenge is not access but attention.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Contrast painting with a song or a novel. In painting, every element is available at once; the experience is not sequential.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q7a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">7</span> According to this lesson, what is the subject matter of an abstract painting such as Rothko's No. 61?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7a" id="q7a">
        <label for="q7a">The sensuous: the visual qualities of color, shape, and line experienced directly.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7b" id="q7b">
        <label for="q7b">Nothing; abstract paintings have no subject matter.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7c" id="q7c">
        <label for="q7c">A hidden landscape.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q7" value="q7d" id="q7d">
        <label for="q7d">A portrait of the artist.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. In abstract painting there is no recognizable subject to decode, so the subject matter is the sensuous itself, the pure visual qualities.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Abstract paintings do have subject matter, defined differently from representational ones. Look for the answer about the pure visual qualities.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q8b">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">8</span> In Frida Kahlo's The Two Fridas, the artery connecting the two hearts is</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8a" id="q8a">
        <label for="q8a">the only part of the painting that is realistic.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8b" id="q8b">
        <label for="q8b">the detail that ties the figures together physically while their clothing and posture hold them apart.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8c" id="q8c">
        <label for="q8c">evidence that the painting is abstract.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q8" value="q8d" id="q8d">
        <label for="q8d">a purely decorative flourish.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. The artery is the painting's most striking detail relationship: it makes the division of the self visible and shows that the two selves are still joined.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Look at the artery's role in the composition. It connects the two figures even as their dress and posture separate them.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q9a">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">9</span> Why does the medium matter in Jacob Lawrence's Migration Series, Panel 1?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9a" id="q9a">
        <label for="q9a">Casein tempera produces flat, opaque color with sharp edges, which gives the figures a graphic quality that emphasizes movement and pattern.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9b" id="q9b">
        <label for="q9b">The medium is irrelevant to the content.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9c" id="q9c">
        <label for="q9c">Watercolor lets the paper show through the figures.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q9" value="q9d" id="q9d">
        <label for="q9d">Oil paint made the faces highly detailed.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. Lawrence's flat color and closed line turn the crowd into a collective force; the same subject in soft oil paint would feel different.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Medium shapes what a painter can do. Casein tempera is flat and opaque, which affects how the crowd of figures reads.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz__question" data-correct="q10d">
    <div class="quiz__question-text"><span class="quiz__number">10</span> In Giotto's Lamentation, the slope of the hillside runs diagonally down toward the faces of Mary and Christ. What is this an example of?</div>
    <ul class="quiz__choices">
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10a" id="q10a">
        <label for="q10a">A medium.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10b" id="q10b">
        <label for="q10b">Texture only.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10c" id="q10c">
        <label for="q10c">A color mixture.</label>
      </li>
      <li class="quiz__choice">
        <input type="radio" name="q10" value="q10d" id="q10d">
        <label for="q10d">Composition: an axis line that guides your eye through the painting.</label>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--correct" style="display:none;">Correct. An axis line is an imaginary line that determines a painting's basic visual direction. Here the diagonal leads your eye to the emotional center of the scene.</div>
    <div class="quiz__feedback quiz__feedback--incorrect" style="display:none;">Think about how your eye moves through the painting. A line that sets that direction is an axis line, and how things are arranged is composition.</div>
  </div>
</div>

